# Two Vercel environment variables. Zero serverless functions (Revision A §9).
#
# THE KEY BELOW MUST BE THE PUBLISHABLE ONE.
#
# Supabase has two key generations and the naming changed, which is the
# usual cause of getting this wrong:
#
#   current:  sb_publishable_...   <- USE THIS (browser-safe)
#             sb_secret_...        <- NEVER here. Server only.
#   legacy:   anon JWT (eyJ...)    <- USE THIS (browser-safe)
#             service_role JWT     <- NEVER here. Server only.
#
# The publishable/anon key is designed for browser use and every table it
# can read is behind an explicit RLS policy (sql/ad4_rls.sql).
#
# A NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable is compiled into the JavaScript every visitor
# downloads. Putting a secret key here publishes it - it then has to be
# ROTATED, not just replaced. AD4 refuses to open a connection with a secret
# key and says so on every page (web/lib/keyGuard.ts), but that does not
# un-publish a key that has already been served.
#
# The secret key belongs in exactly two places: the GitHub Actions secret
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, and your n8n Config nodes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://jittmxhzgqpifitwupss.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace_with_the_PUBLISHABLE_key
